# Condition checker cron line (Ref #346 PR 5).
#
# NOT INSTALLED. Install only with Bucket's approval: the checker runs every
# 5 minutes, reads pm2/Supabase/disk and writes to the shared JSONL error
# log, so it should not appear on the VPS without a decision.
#
# Log-only condition checks: no published narrative > 2h, no editor draft
# > 3h, > 5 app restarts in 15 min, 3 consecutive failed Supabase health
# probes, missing Supabase env (config_missing), disk used > 80%. Breaches
# land in ~/myboon-logs/errors.jsonl (kinds publish_stale / draft_stale /
# restart_burst / supabase_health_failed / config_missing / disk_high);
# stopped PM2 apps keep their staleness checks silent.
*/5 * * * * cd /home/ubuntu/myboon && pnpm --filter @myboon/collectors pipeline-store:check >> /home/ubuntu/myboon-logs/condition-check.cron.log 2>&1

# Lane-store prune cron line (Ref #346 PR 6).
#
# NOT INSTALLED. Install only with Bucket's approval, and only AFTER the
# #377 managed-entity backfill has completed and the same command has been run
# as a dry run (no --apply) with its JSON reviewed: this prune deletes old
# terminal rows from the two lane SQLite stores (news-lane.sqlite /
# polymarket-lane.sqlite). 14-day retention for terminal run / research rows,
# 7-day retention for delivered outbox rows; news_candidate_observations (the
# news dedupe memory: pruning a settled observation would re-admit a
# still-listed article as new_candidate and get it researched and placed a
# second time), pipeline_watchlist, undelivered outbox rows, non-terminal rows
# and failed / dead-letter rows are never deleted. Statuses and safety rules:
# packages/collectors/src/lane-store/prune.ts. A lane whose file is missing is
# skipped, never created.
35 4 * * * cd /home/ubuntu/myboon && pnpm --filter @myboon/collectors lane-store:prune -- --apply >> /home/ubuntu/myboon-logs/lane-store-prune.cron.log 2>&1

# Backup-file prune cron lines (Ref #346: cap backups to 1-2 per store).
#
# NOT INSTALLED. Install only with Bucket's approval, and only AFTER both
# commands below have been run as a dry run (without --apply) with their JSON
# audited and every candidateDeletePaths entry reviewed.
#
# `pipeline-store:backup` writes online backup FILES to PIPELINE_BACKUP_DIR,
# defaulting to packages/collectors/.data/backups - on this VPS that is
# /home/ubuntu/myboon/packages/collectors/.data/backups (the ops docs under
# docs/modules/entity-manager/operations reference that path). If
# PIPELINE_BACKUP_DIR is set on the VPS, use that directory in the lines
# below instead.
#
# pipeline-store:backup:prune deletes old backup files, not SQLite rows. It
# matches `pipeline-<timestamp>.sqlite` / `news-<timestamp>.sqlite` files in
# --backup-dir (prefix 'pipeline-' / 'news-', pruneOldBackups in
# src/pipeline-store/backup.ts), keeps the newest --keep files per store,
# deletes at most --limit files per run oldest-first, and removes a backup's
# companion manifest (<backup>.sqlite.manifest.json next to the file) only
# when that backup file is a deletion candidate. Dry run by default; only
# --apply deletes, and --backup-dir must be absolute.
#
# Dry-run first, review candidateDeletePaths, then repeat with --apply:
#   pnpm --filter @myboon/collectors pipeline-store:backup:prune -- \
#     --store pipeline --backup-dir /home/ubuntu/myboon/packages/collectors/.data/backups --keep 2 --limit 10
#   pnpm --filter @myboon/collectors pipeline-store:backup:prune -- \
#     --store news --backup-dir /home/ubuntu/myboon/packages/collectors/.data/backups --keep 2 --limit 10
#
# Scheduled at 04:50 / 04:55 so neither collides with the 04:35 lane prune.
50 4 * * * cd /home/ubuntu/myboon && pnpm --filter @myboon/collectors pipeline-store:backup:prune -- --store pipeline --backup-dir /home/ubuntu/myboon/packages/collectors/.data/backups --keep 2 --limit 10 --apply >> /home/ubuntu/myboon-logs/backup-prune.cron.log 2>&1
55 4 * * * cd /home/ubuntu/myboon && pnpm --filter @myboon/collectors pipeline-store:backup:prune -- --store news --backup-dir /home/ubuntu/myboon/packages/collectors/.data/backups --keep 2 --limit 10 --apply >> /home/ubuntu/myboon-logs/backup-prune.cron.log 2>&1